counterfactuals.output:
A downhole tool comprising:

a mandrel defining a longitudinal tool axis;

a bidirectional slip frame disposed about the mandrel, the bidirectional slip frame including a center ring and a plurality of slats extending axially from the center ring, the plurality of slats being radially spaced about the longitudinal tool axis;

a plurality of paired slots formed between adjacent ones of the plurality of slats on opposing axial sides of the center ring; and

a plurality of gripping banks respectively received in the paired slots, each gripping bank being configured for radial movement relative to the bidirectional slip frame between a retracted position and an expanded position;

wherein, in the expanded position, the gripping banks extend radially outward from the bidirectional slip frame to engage an inner wall of a casing, and wherein the bidirectional slip frame supports the gripping banks to resist axial movement of the downhole tool in either longitudinal direction within the casing.
